00:22:26,700 --> 00:22:27,460
point was

571
00:22:27,670 --> 00:22:28,780
the moment you think

572
00:22:28,780 --> 00:22:29,980
you're sacrificing for someone,

573
00:22:29,980 --> 00:22:30,700
you start feeling

574
00:22:30,700 --> 00:22:32,140
like some kind of hero.

575
00:22:32,710 --> 00:22:34,030
I get what you mean.

576
00:22:34,030 --> 00:22:36,740
But maybe they just want your company.

577
00:22:36,740 --> 00:22:38,870
They never asked you
to sacrifice so much.

578
00:22:40,380 --> 00:22:44,060
So she said they
could give freely to each other.

579
00:22:44,310 --> 00:22:45,550
But they shouldn't

580
00:22:45,550 --> 00:22:47,790
look back and call it a sacrifice.

581
00:22:49,310 --> 00:22:49,630
I think

582
00:22:49,630 --> 00:22:50,980
that also ties

583
00:22:50,980 --> 00:22:52,660
into Independent Love

584
00:22:52,660 --> 00:22:54,180
just a little.

585
00:22:54,870 --> 00:22:55,670
Absolutely.

586
00:22:55,670 --> 00:22:56,190
Right?

587
00:22:56,190 --> 00:22:57,590
Exactly.

588
00:22:57,590 --> 00:22:58,660
Yeah, I think

589
00:22:58,660 --> 00:23:00,660
it's all about how you see it.

590
00:23:00,660 --> 00:23:02,220
I'm giving because I want to.

591
00:23:02,220 --> 00:23:03,460
It's not a sacrifice.

592
00:23:03,830 --> 00:23:05,470
Sacrifice implies I'm losing something.

593
00:23:05,750 --> 00:23:06,420
Like I'm so noble

594
00:23:06,420 --> 00:23:06,980
for your sake.

595
00:23:06,980 --> 00:23:07,940
But love isn't

596
00:23:07,940 --> 00:23:08,860
about being noble.

597
00:23:09,190 --> 00:23:10,030
Yeah, exactly.

